* sg13g2-lc-pll :: sim/noise-probe -- DR-007 method-N feasibility probe.
* ONE local ngspice -b, nominal corner (mos_tt / hbt_typ), 27 C, nominal 3.3 V.
* It answers three yes/no questions and nothing else. It is NOT a bench: one operating
* point, one corner, no negative control, no corner grid, not in sim/testbench-inventory.json.
* The method-N bench is issue #253.
*
*   (a) Units calibration. A 1 kohm resistor read through a noiseless unity VCVS. If
*       ngspice's onoise_spectrum is an amplitude density in V/sqrt(Hz) it must read
*       sqrt(4kTR) = 4.0714e-9 at 300.15 K; if it were a power density in V^2/Hz it would
*       read 1.6576e-17. This fixes the units every other number in the record is in.
*   (b) Does .noise return device noise for the charge pump's sg13_hv_nmos / sg13_hv_pmos
*       (PSP103 through the OSDI module)? cp.spice contains no resistors, so any non-zero
*       output noise is device noise. The CP output current is sensed by a 0 V source plus
*       a 1 V/A CCVS -- both noiseless -- so v(ns) numerically equals the CP's short-circuit
*       output current noise in A/sqrt(Hz). The output is held at Vctrl by an ideal source:
*       the loop filter is deliberately absent (the method-L model applies its shaping, and
*       R1's thermal noise is already a separate model term; including it here would
*       double-count it).
*   (b2) What are the per-leg DC currents at that same operating point? Three further
*       copies of cp, each with its own output forced to the same Vctrl through its own
*       noiseless 0 V sense and its own IREF: UP asserted alone (the leg that sources),
*       DN asserted alone (the leg that sinks), and neither asserted (both tails dumped).
*       These let the record show residual = I_up - I_dn instead of asserting it against
*       figures from another run, and they separate the balanced steering state from the
*       both-dumped state, whose residual is also small. DR-007 section 5 field 3 requires
*       them beside the residual. They carry no `ac` drive and share only the ideal VDD and
*       ground nodes with copy (b), so they do not enter its noise analysis.
*   (c) Does .noise return device noise for npn13G2v (VBIC)? Same noiseless current sense
*       on the collector of a common-emitter device at VBE = 0.85 V.
*
* Operating point for (b): UP and DN both asserted, i.e. both legs steering their tail
* current to VOUT. That is the UP/DN reset-overlap state the charge pump is in during t_on
* in lock, and it is the state DR-007 defines method N's operating point as.
*
* Placeholders (@@...@@) are substituted by hand (see sim/noise-probe/README.md);
* nothing else is substituted.
.lib @@MODELS_DIR@@/cornerMOShv.lib mos_tt
.lib @@MODELS_DIR@@/cornerHBT.lib hbt_typ
.option scale=1 temp=27
.include @@CP_NETLIST@@

* (a) units calibration
RCAL n1 0 1k
ICAL 0 n1 dc 0 ac 1
ECAL nr 0 n1 0 1

* (b) charge pump, both legs steered to VOUT, output held at Vctrl = 2.0 V,
*     IREF = 20 uA (I_cp ~ 200 uA, spec row 6 typical)
VDD vdd 0 3.3
VHI hi 0 3.3
VCTRL vc 0 2.0
VSENSE vout vc 0
HSENS ns 0 VSENSE 1
IREF vdd iref dc 20u ac 1
XCP hi hi iref vout vdd 0 cp

* (b2) per-leg DC currents, same netlist, same corner, same forced Vctrl = 2.0 V and
*      IREF = 20 uA. DC only: no ac drive, so these copies are not in (b)'s noise analysis.
VLO lo 0 0
VCTRLU vcu 0 2.0
VSENSEU voutu vcu 0
IREFU vdd irefu dc 20u
XCPU hi lo irefu voutu vdd 0 cp

VCTRLD vcd 0 2.0
VSENSED voutd vcd 0
IREFD vdd irefd dc 20u
XCPD lo hi irefd voutd vdd 0 cp

VCTRLZ vcz 0 2.0
VSENSEZ voutz vcz 0
IREFZ vdd irefz dc 20u
XCPZ lo lo irefz voutz vdd 0 cp

* (c) npn13G2v common emitter at VBE = 0.85 V
VCC vcc 0 3.3
VB  b 0 0.85
VSENSEQ vcc c 0
HSENSQ nh 0 VSENSEQ 1
IBQ 0 bx dc 0 ac 1
VBX bx b 0
XQ1 c b 0 0 npn13G2v Nx=1 El=1

.control
pre_osdi @@OSDI_PSP@@
pre_osdi @@OSDI_PSP_NQS@@
op
print i(VSENSE) i(VSENSEQ)
echo "--- (b2) per-leg DC currents: UP alone, DN alone, both dumped ---"
print i(VSENSEU) i(VSENSED) i(VSENSEZ)
echo "--- (a) calibration: 1 kohm, expect sqrt(4kTR) = 4.0714e-9 V/sqrt(Hz) ---"
noise v(nr) ICAL lin 2 1k 10k 1
setplot noise1
print onoise_spectrum
destroy all
echo "--- (b) charge pump output current noise, A/sqrt(Hz) ---"
noise v(ns) IREF dec 10 1e4 1e7 1
setplot noise1
wrdata @@DATA_OUT@@ onoise_spectrum
print onoise_spectrum
destroy all
echo "--- (c) npn13G2v collector current noise, A/sqrt(Hz) ---"
noise v(nh) IBQ dec 2 1e4 1e7 1
setplot noise1
print onoise_spectrum
.endc
.end
